From ec5b8a2581c2e6a306198421f122305115ad837c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:05:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] [SDL3-DOS] dos: patch 0141 -- count SB ring writes that
 overrun unplayed audio

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice copies each mixed chunk
into the ISR ring with no room check of its own. Room is checked only in
DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice, which only SDL's background thread loop
(while (Iterate()) WaitDevice()) runs. SDL_DOSAudioPump() (patch 0067)
calls SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate() directly, with no WaitDevice, and
looks at room only afterwards, for its return value. A port that pumps
while the ring is full therefore overwrites the chunk the IRQ handler
plays next -- audible as a skip, and a clip "finishes" in engine time
well before it has played. Nothing counted that event, so whether it
happens, and whether a fix for it works, could only be argued from
source, not measured.

How it surfaced (dosags, PLAN.md step 8, "UR1", 2026-09-22):
SDL_DOSAudioRingFillMs() read 232 -> 4086 ms against a 743 ms ring. The
fill is ring_write - isr_ring_read with both cursors monotonic, so a
value above ring_size means the writer lapped the reader. That UR1 run
was under DOSBox-X with its Sound Blaster switched off (dosbox-run.sh's
-silent, before --sb-live existed), so the ISR never drained and the
figure's size says nothing about a real device; the lap itself is still
a write over unplayed data, which is what this counts.

WHAT: a monotonic dos_port_audio_ring_overwrite_count
(SDL_dos_audio_synth.c, beside the other per-IRQ audio counters),
incremented in PlayDevice once per write where
(ring_write - isr_ring_read) + buffer_size > ring_size, before the copy.
Counting only; behaviour is unchanged. The ISR may advance isr_ring_read
between the check and the copy, so the count can over-state by a write
that raced a drain, never under-state. A port reads it through the
extern in SDL_dos_audio_synth.h, as it does the other counters there.
The fix is the next patch (0142), so the "before" is measurable on the
same counter.

Measured with it (dosags, DOSBox-X --sb-live equivalent: no -silent, SB
detection on; 5 Days a Stranger in play, OPL3 music, SB PCM SFX; cells
OVW1/OVW3): overwrites=38 and 19, peak fill 1625 and 1578 ms against
743. Emulator only; the counter's real-hardware reading is part of a
hardware re-run still pending.

Source: dosags patches/SDL/0190 (From 0a7ec940ef43), re-derived here
against the hub series (applies at a line offset only; the dosags-only
patches between 0140 and 0190 do not touch these functions). Comment
tags renumbered 0190 -> 0141.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
